ston  which is where I live coming in where  half of the units are going to be  reserved for people with family incomes  household incomes under $70,000 for  example meaning it could be two people  making $30,000  I think that all those things are good  and I think that the more I read and  since last week's live calls I've  actually been reading a lot more because  we got a question about this about what  can be done to deal with the hugely  exploded housing prices supply is  actually a big part of it there are  other regulatory things that can be done  and there's many other ideas but you've  got to increase the supply of housing  that actually is a big part of it and  it's got to be relatively affordable  housing so I am in favor of the Y MB  movement yes in my backyard although I  don't literally have a backyard because  there's other apartments there but if I  had a backyard I would say go ahead and  build there why not thanks to everybody  who submitted questions we've got a  great bonus show for you today get  access to the bonus show by becoming a  member at join pakman.com or becoming a  patron at patreon.com slash david pakman  show
 

